# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# solana_agents — environment
#
# The NVIDIA key is read from the repository-root .env (../../.env), which the
# demo scripts and docker compose both load. Copy your key there:
#
#   NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...        # free key at https://build.nvidia.com
#
# This file documents every knob. Copy it to .env in THIS directory to override
# settings for a local run.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LLM (NVIDIA NIM) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for the `solo` tool-calling demo and for the orchestrator's final
# synthesis. The chain specialists read chains WITHOUT a key — so the mesh still
# produces on-chain facts with no key; the key only buys a polished answer.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...

# Override the chat model (a listed model is not always callable — probe first):
NVIDIA_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b

# ── Which network a specialist serves ────────────────────────────────────────
# A specialist's ROLE is the network it serves. Built-in presets:
#
#   SVM (Solana-like):  solana-mainnet  solana-testnet  solana-devnet
#                       eclipse         sonic-testnet
#   EVM:                ethereum        base            polygon
#
#   ROLE=solana-testnet   # → https://api.testnet.solana.com
#   ROLE=eclipse          # → https://mainnetbeta-rpc.eclipse.xyz   (SVM L2)
#
# A custom chain needs CHAIN_KIND + RPC_URL (ROLE becomes its display label):
#   ROLE=my-svm  CHAIN_KIND=svm  RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8899   # local validator
#   ROLE=arbitrum CHAIN_KIND=evm RPC_URL=https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc
#
# RPC_URL also overrides a preset's default endpoint (e.g. your own provider URL).
# RPC_URL=
# CHAIN_KIND=svm

# ── solo demo endpoints ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single-process `solo` agent reads one SVM + one EVM endpoint:
SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
EVM_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com

# ── Demo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Networks the demo.sh script spins up (one specialist per entry):
# CHAINS=solana-testnet eclipse sonic-testnet ethereum
#
# The question the CLIENT (or the `solo` agent) asks. Named QUESTION — NOT
# PROMPT — so it doesn't collide with the shell's own $PROMPT in zsh. Include a
# base58 address and/or a 0x address to make specialists fetch balances.
# QUESTION=Compare the slots and genesis hashes of every network you can reach.

# ── libp2p transport ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when mDNS multicast is blocked (restricted Wi-Fi/VPN/CI). Seed one
# connection and gossip discovery still flows. Not needed on the Docker bridge.
# The demo scripts set these for you (orchestrator is the seed on tcp/4201).
# LISTEN=/ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/0
# BOOTSTRAP=/ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4201

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUST_LOG=info,solana_agents=info
